🔥✌️My understanding of Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) vs. SEO👇

I find the many discussions on the subject of naming a bit excessive. I have the feeling that many people are currently more concerned with this discussion than with how to optimize for the new AI systems in practice.

Nevertheless, I would like to briefly present my classification of the terms here.

GEO is the intersection of SEO, PR, and branding. Depending on the objective, i.e., improving brand mentions or optimizing citability, the focus is on one area or the other.

These two main objectives of GEO require different skills, ressources and strategies.

Optimizing citability consists largely of SEO as we know it, plus new aspects such as query fan out and passage-based retrieval, which need to be taken into account. Here are my two detailed articles on these two new topics.

From Query Refinement to Query Fan-Out: Search in times of generative AI and AI Agents: https://lnkd.in/e6GQijHA

From Phrase Indexing to Generative Passage Retrieval and how to optimize LLM Readability and Chunk Relevance
https://lnkd.in/emXWFRY4

Optimizing brand mentions, or what I call brand context optimization, consists largely of targeted online PR and branding to strengthen the positioning of brands in relevant subject areas and USPs.

And there is another aspect I must mention here from an agency perspective. I think it is ignorant not to use terms like GEO or LLMO when they are used in the market.

For brand context optimization, we need access to resources from branding and PR, which in my experience is often not possible under the banner of SEO. This is another reason why one should not be resistant to new terminology.